REFUTED — two independent guards. The file's own comment records the claim verbatim as known and unreached: packages/ui/src/components/context-menu/context-menu-merge.ts:39-42 `// Latent, unreachable today: the separator keys this mints can collide with a
	// host that pre-built \`defaults\` through the public \`mergeContextMenuItems\`
	// and fed the result back in, producing duplicate React keys. No in-repo
	// consumer composes them that way.` And the public signatures refuse the composition: context-menu-merge.ts:12 `export function mergeContextMenuItems(groups: ContextMenuEntry[][]): ContextMenuEntry[] {` against :31-34 `export function resolveContextMenuEntries(
	config: ContextMenuConfig | undefined,
	defaults: ContextMenuItem[],
): ContextMenuEntry[] {` — a `ContextMenuEntry[]` is not assignable to `ContextMenuItem[]`, because packages/ui/src/components/context-menu/types.ts:32-36 `export type ContextMenuSeparator = {` … `separator: true
}` supplies no `label` and types.ts:18 `label: ReactNode` is required. The same guard sits on the component prop: packages/ui/src/components/context-menu/context-menu.tsx:15 `defaults?: ContextMenuItem[]`.

NARROWED — the flip is confirmed, but "jumps to the shadow internal value (step 0)" is guarded whenever the owner drove the value through the widget. packages/ui/src/hooks/use-controllable.ts:59-63 `// Written even while controlled: \`value !== undefined\` decides
		// controlled-ness per render, so a controlled consumer that clears to
		// \`undefined\` flips the hook to uncontrolled; the shadow keeps that
		// flip resolving to the last committed value instead of a stale one.
		setInternalValue(normalized)`. Every step click routes through that setter (`stepper.tsx:137 onValueChange: interactive ? setCurrent : undefined`), so the shadow already holds the last committed index and the stepper stays where it was. Step 0 appears only where the shadow was never written — an owner that moved `value` programmatically and never let the widget commit — so the "jumps to step 0" half is the narrower case, not the general one. The confirmed part is the silent controlled-to-uncontrolled flip and the absence of any `null` arm (`stepper.tsx:17 value?: number`).
